Infrastructure: SDD

Purpose:
  Infrastructure technology catalog with deployment targets, containerization,
  orchestration, and IaC options. Root stack/ defines reusable infrastructure
  knowledge; projects/vkard.az/stack/ stores the selected infrastructure for the project.

Catalog:
  Docker:
    Type: Containerization
    Pros:
      - Standardized packaging
      - Consistent environments
      - Rapid deployment
      - Resource efficiency
    Cons:
      - Learning curve
      - Security surface
      - Storage overhead
    BestFor:
      - All containerized deployments
      - Microservices
      - Development environments
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple single-binary deployments

  Kubernetes:
    Type: Orchestration
    Pros:
      - Auto-scaling
      - Self-healing
      - Service discovery
      - Rolling updates
    Cons:
      - High complexity
      - Operational overhead
      - Overkill for small projects
    BestFor:
      - Large microservice deployments
      - High availability requirements
      - Auto-scaling needs
    AvoidWhen:
      - Small projects (prefer Docker Compose)

  Nomad:
    Type: Orchestration
    Pros:
      - Simpler than Kubernetes
      - Flexible (VMs, containers)
      - HashiCorp ecosystem
    Cons:
      - Smaller ecosystem
      - Less community support
    BestFor:
      - HashiCorp shops
      - Mixed workloads
    AvoidWhen:
      - Teams with Kubernetes experience

  Terraform:
    Type: IaC
    Pros:
      - Multi-cloud
      - Declarative
      - Large provider ecosystem
      - State management
    Cons:
      - State file management
      - Learning curve
    BestFor:
      - Infrastructure automation
      - Multi-cloud deployments
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple deployments

  Ansible:
    Type: Configuration Management
    Pros:
      - Agentless
      - Simple YAML
      - Large ecosystem
    Cons:
      - Slower execution
      - Less declarative than Terraform
    BestFor:
      - Configuration management
      - Legacy infrastructure
    AvoidWhen:
      - Cloud-native IaC

  VPS:
    Type: Bare Metal / VPS
    Pros:
      - Simple
      - Full control
      - Low cost for small projects
    Cons:
      - Manual scaling
      - No built-in HA
    BestFor:
      - Small projects
      - Prototypes
      - Low traffic
    AvoidWhen:
      - High availability requirements

  AWS:
    Type: Cloud Provider
    Pros:
      - Comprehensive services
      - Global infrastructure
      - Strong ecosystem
    Cons:
      - Complex pricing
      - Vendor lock-in
      - Learning curve
    BestFor:
      - Enterprise cloud
      - Global scale
      - Managed services
    AvoidWhen:
      - Multi-cloud requirements

  GCP:
    Type: Cloud Provider
    Pros:
      - Strong data/AI services
      - Kubernetes-native
      - Global network
    Cons:
      - Smaller ecosystem than AWS
      - Less enterprise adoption
    BestFor:
      - Data-heavy workloads
      - Kubernetes-native
    AvoidWhen:
      - AWS expertise exists

  Azure:
    Type: Cloud Provider
    Pros:
      - Enterprise integration
      - Windows support
      - Hybrid cloud
    Cons:
      - Complex pricing
      - Inconsistent UX
    BestFor:
      - Enterprise Microsoft shops
      - Hybrid cloud
    AvoidWhen:
      - Non-Microsoft ecosystems

SelectionRules:
  - Scale: project size and traffic expectations
  - Complexity: team operational capability
  - Cost: infrastructure budget constraints
  - Availability: uptime requirements
  - Compliance: regulatory requirements
  - TeamFit: existing infrastructure expertise

TechnologyScore:
  Scale: 0-25
  Complexity: 0-20
  Cost: 0-15
  Availability: 0-15
  Compliance: 0-10
  TeamFit: 0-15

State: +
  